## Day-8:learning linux commands

#find (advanced commands)
- dd if=dev/zero of =large.bin bs=1k count=100
->It creates a 100KB FILE for process
- find . -size +50k
-> find files more than 50kb
- find . -size -50k
-> find files less than 50kb
similarly
- find . -empty
- find . -mtime -1
- find . -mtime +7

#Delete matching files 
- find . -name "*.log" -delete
-> Delete all matching log files

##tar command
- tar -cvf project.tar f1.txt f2.txt f3.txt
- tar -tvf project.tar
- tar -xvf project.tar
(important symbols)
c-create a new archive
v-verbose
f-filename of archive
x-extract

# gzip(compresses the file)
- gzip f1 for compression
- gunzip f1.gz for decompression
- gzip -k sample.txt for keeping both original and compressed files
